## Compile typed SPARQL value FILTERs into SQL (#210)
================================================================================

Context: Knowledge Graph SPARQL queries of the form `?x rdf:type :Class` plus
an attribute triple and `FILTER(STR(?v) = "…")` / `CONTAINS(LCASE(STR(?v)), …)`
passed validation but generated `WHERE 1=1`. Results were unfiltered. Typed
BGPs now compile those filters; unmapped filters fail closed.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/w3c/sparql/SparqlValueFilterSql.py
   Extract SQL compilation for string FILTERs; apply them on typed BGPs.
2. src/back/core/w3c/sparql/SparqlTranslator.py
   Call the compiler from the typed SQL path; reuse it on generic triples.
3. src/back/core/w3c/sparql/__init__.py
   Re-export SparqlValueFilterSql.
4. tests/back/core/w3c/sparql/test_sparql_translator_units.py
   Assert each accepted FILTER shape reaches SQL; unmapped filters raise.
5. tests/units/core/test_sql_literal_escaping.py
   Point value-filter escape tests at SparqlValueFilterSql.
6. docs/architecture.md
   Note that typed BGP string FILTERs compile to SQL.

Modified files:
- src/back/core/w3c/sparql/SparqlValueFilterSql.py
- src/back/core/w3c/sparql/SparqlTranslator.py
